   "source": [
    "## Introducción\n",
    "\n",
    "La normalización Min-Max escala valores al intervalo [0, 1]. La fórmula es (x - min) / (max - min). Si todos los valores son iguales, devuelve ceros para evitar división por cero.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Objetivos de Aprendizaje\n",
    "\n",
    "- Implementar Min-Max scaling sin NumPy\n",
    "- Aplicar operaciones de álgebra lineal\n",
    "- Resolver problemas prácticos de Data Science\n",
    "- Combinar múltiples operaciones de arrays"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "min-max-scale",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Normalización Min-Max\n",
    "\n",
    "> Escala valores al intervalo [0, 1] usando la fórmula: (x - min) / (max - min). Si todos los valores son iguales, devuelve ceros."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "min-max-code",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def min_max_scale(values):\n",
    "    low, high = min(values), max(values)\n",
    "    if low == high:\n",
    "        return [0 for _ in values]\n",
    "    return [(value - low) / (high - low) for value in values]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(min_max_scale([2, 4, 6]))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nCon NumPy:\")\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "arr = np.array([2, 4, 6])\n",
    "print((arr - arr.min()) / (arr.max() - arr.min()))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "distance-matrix",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Matriz de Distancias Euclidiana\n",
    "\n",
    "> Calcular la distancia entre todos los pares de puntos en un dataset. La distancia euclidiana entre dos puntos es la raíz cuadrada de la suma de diferencias al cuadrado."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "distance-code",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"=== Matriz de Distancias ===\")\n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "\n",
    "def euclidean_distance(p1, p2):\n",
    "    return np.sqrt(np.sum((p1 - p2) ** 2))\n",
    "\n",
    "def distance_matrix(points):\n",
    "    n = len(points)\n",
    "    dist = np.zeros((n, n))\n",
    "    for i in range(n):\n",
    "        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n",
    "            d = euclidean_distance(points[i], points[j])\n",
    "            dist[i, j] = d\n",
    "            dist[j, i] = d\n",
    "    return dist\n",
    "\n",
    "points = np.array([[0, 0], [3, 4], [6, 8]])\n",
    "print(\"Puntos:\", points)\n",
    "print(\"\\nMatriz de distancias:\")\n",
    "print(distance_matrix(points))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type":="markdown",
   "id": "matrix-multiplication",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Multiplicación de Matrices Manual\n",
    "\n",
    "> Implementar multiplicación de matrices sin usar NumPy. El elemento (i,j) de la resultado es la suma de productos de la fila i de A con la columna j de B."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "matmul-code",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"=== Multiplicación de Matrices ===\")\n",
    "\n",
    "def matrix_multiply(A, B):\n",
    "    n = len(A)\n",
    "    m = len(B[0])\n",
    "    p = len(B)\n",
    "    result = [[0] * m for _ in range(n)]\n",
    "    for i in range(n):\n",
    "        for j in range(m):\n",
    "            for k in range(p):\n",
    "                result[i][j] += A[i][k] * B[k][j]\n",
    "    return result\n",
    "\n",
    "A = [[1, 2], [3, 4]]\n",
    "B = [[5, 6], [7, 8]]\n",
    "print(\"A:\", A)\n",
    "print(\"B:\", B)\n",
    "print(\"A @ B:\", matrix_multiply(A, B))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nCon NumPy:\")\n",
    "print(np.array(A) @ np.array(B))"
   ]
  },
  {
