   "source": [
    "## PCA (Análisis de Componentes Principales)\n",
    "\n",
    "> PCA reduce la dimensionalidad encontrando las direcciones de máxima varianza en los datos. NumPy facilita el cálculo de autovalores y autovectores."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "pca-code",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"=== PCA Simplificado ===\")\n",
    "\n",
    "datos = np.array([[2.5, 2.4], [0.5, 0.7], [2.2, 2.9], [1.9, 2.2],\n",
    "                   [3.1, 3.0], [2.3, 2.7], [2, 1.6], [1, 1.1],\n",
    "                   [1.5, 1.6], [1.1, 0.9]])\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Datos originales (10 muestras, 2 features):\")\n",
    "print(datos)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nCentrar los datos (restar media):\")\n",
    "centrado = datos - datos.mean(axis=0)\n",
    "print(centrado)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nAutovalores y autovectores de la matriz de covarianza:\")\n",
    "cov = np.cov(centrado.T)\n",
    "autovalores, autovectores = np.linalg.eig(cov)\n",
    "print(f\"Autovalores: {autovalores}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Autovectores:\\n{autovectores}\")"
   ]
  },
